{
  "format": "lumenet-project",
  "version": 4,
  "notes": "<div><font size=\"5\"><b>Moving heads</b></font></div><div>Two moving heads from the fixture library (American DJ Inno Pocket Spot, 9 channels), a front wash and a hazer. The memories hold where the heads point, with their color and gobo.</div><div><b><font color=\"#ffb020\">What is in it</font></b></div><ul><li>The kind of light came from the fixture library: on <b>Stage</b>, <b>Edit</b>, a head, <b>Kind</b>. The desk knows its pan, tilt, color wheel, gobo wheel, shutter and dimmer.</li><li>Memories 1 to 4: positions with a color: center stage, crossed beams in red, over the audience in blue, gobos on the floor.</li><li>Memory 5: the heads swing between memories 2 and 3. Memory 6: haze.</li><li>The stack goes through the positions.</li></ul><div><b><font color=\"#ffb020\">Try it</font></b></div><ol><li>Open <b>Fixtures</b> and choose <b>Head left</b>: move it on the pad (pan and tilt), pick a slot of its color wheel, open it with its fader.</li><li>Push the fader of memory 2 up: the heads take the position and the color it holds. Then memory 3: the latest one takes the heads.</li><li>Take memory 3 down again: the heads go back to memory 2, which took them before.</li><li>Press <b>Stack</b> and <b>Play</b> through the positions.</li></ol><div>Pan, tilt and the wheels go to whatever moved them last; only the light (the dimmer) adds up, and only it follows <b>Master</b> and <b>Blackout</b>.</div>",
